## Critical Rules (Always Follow)

All rules in the detailed files listed above are critical and must be followed. See the specific rule files for comprehensive guidelines on:
- Design principles (SOLID, PLK, Composition over Inheritance, KISS, YAGNI) and controller design
- Code quality standards (error handling, null safety, file organization, async patterns)
- Code smells to avoid (long methods/classes, too many dependencies, static classes)
- Testing standards (test maintenance, naming conventions, mocking, assertions)
- If your changes require modifications to `.cursor/docs/structure_analysis.md`, make the necessary updates there. 
For the full set of rules, refer to the detailed rule files in `.cursor/rules/`

